<h2>Crashes</h2>
<p>If a worker process dies in the middle of a scenario, only that scenario fails and the lane starts a new process. Its <code>After</code> hooks do not run. Set <code>retry.workerCrash</code> to retry the scenario on a fresh process. If a worker cannot start at all, the run stops.</p>

<h2>Sharing data between workers</h2>
<p>Things that are per process with the process pool:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>ctx.feature</code> and <code>ctx.groups</code> stores, and module-level variables.</li>
  <li>Feature, group and rule hooks. They run once in each process that runs a member.</li>
</ul>
<p>To share a value, use <code>ctx.export</code> and <code>ctx.from</code> (see <a href="dependencies.html">Dependencies</a>), or an external system such as a database.</p>
<aside class="callout tip"><p class="callout-title">Tip</p><p>Start with the inline pool. Switch to <code>process</code> when browser tests become the bottleneck or you need crash isolation.</p></aside>
